Subject: [PATCH] BRINGUP: iommu/qcom: Write the BFB table by default, log ACTLR

0041's BFB table made the GPU SMMU's table walk work (G6 passes), so
write it on every resume by default; qcom_iommu.bfb=0 still turns it
off. Also log the bank's ACTLR before the restore: it reads 0x70000000
(BPRCOSH/BPRCISH/BPRCNSH, what the vendor kernel sets) even after a power
collapse, so ACTLR needs no programming.

diff --git a/drivers/iommu/arm/arm-smmu/qcom_iommu.c b/drivers/iommu/arm/arm-smmu/qcom_iommu.c
--- a/drivers/iommu/arm/arm-smmu/qcom_iommu.c	2026-10-18 18:13:26.686223721 -0600
+++ b/drivers/iommu/arm/arm-smmu/qcom_iommu.c	2026-10-18 18:13:26.696420168 -0600
@@ -66,9 +66,9 @@
  * programmed the SMMU, on every first attach after power-up. Values from
  * the vendor msm8994-iommu.dtsi kgsl_iommu node.
  */
-static bool bfb;
+static bool bfb = true;
 module_param(bfb, bool, 0644);
-MODULE_PARM_DESC(bfb, "Write the MSM8994 GPU SMMU BFB table on resume");
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(bfb, "Write the MSM8994 GPU SMMU BFB table on resume (default on)");
 
 #define QCOM_IOMMU_BFB_BASE	0x2000
 #define QCOM_IOMMU_BFB_SIZE	0x1000
@@ -1287,8 +1287,9 @@
 		if (!ctx || !ctx->domain || ctx->secured_ctx)
 			continue;
 
-		dev_info(dev, "iommu pm: ctx %u SCTLR 0x%08x before restore\n",
-			 ctx->asid, iommu_readl(ctx, ARM_SMMU_CB_SCTLR));
+		dev_info(dev, "iommu pm: ctx %u SCTLR 0x%08x ACTLR 0x%08x before restore\n",
+			 ctx->asid, iommu_readl(ctx, ARM_SMMU_CB_SCTLR),
+			 iommu_readl(ctx, ARM_SMMU_CB_ACTLR));
 		qcom_iommu_program_ctx(ctx);
 		dev_info(dev, "iommu pm: ctx %u SCTLR 0x%08x restored\n",
 			 ctx->asid, iommu_readl(ctx, ARM_SMMU_CB_SCTLR));
